  "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\u03a0$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,\u03a0:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$",
